<title>FRANCE: French Nov M3 money supply grew 1.3 percent.</title>
<headline>French Nov M3 money supply grew 1.3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of France gave the following money supply figures (the year-on-year change is expressed as an average centred on the previous month)</p>
<p> Money measure  Billions   Monthly change    12-month change</p>
<p>(end-Nov)	 (unadj)     (adjusted)	   Nov	 Oct</p>
<p>    M1	    1,654.6	  3.1		 5.4	 5.5</p>
<p>    M2	    3,147.8	  2.2		 7.3	 7.4</p>
<p>    M3	    5,260.0	  1.3		-1.1	-0.9</p>
<p>    M4	    5,356.4	  1.3		-0.7	-0.6</p>
<p>Investment</p>
<p>    P1	    1,858.8	  0.8		18.3	18.4</p>
<p> Credit measure		billions	   Year-on-Year change</p>
<p>  (end-Oct)		    (unadj)	   Oct     Sep	Aug</p>
<p> Total domestic debt	10,869.2	   3.6     3.5	3.9</p>
<p> Total credits to economy  6,331.1	  -0.3    -0.1	0.1</p>
<p> Bank credits to economy   3,577.0	   0.0     0.1	0.6</p>
<p>The Bank said October M3 fell a revised 0.8 percent, giving a year-on-year fall of 0.9 percent. It said on December 6 that M3 fell 1.0 percent in October, giving a year-on-year fall of 0.4 percent.</p>
<p>The central bank is targeting M3 growth of roughly five percent a year on average over the next few years.</p>
<p>It is using total domestic debt as a secondary monitoring tool.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
